  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "Production workbench",
    "overview": "The existing browser workbench is compact and utilitarian. System typography, bordered episode buttons and familiar Mantine controls keep production records readable without decorative imagery. Teal identifies the product and some interactions; episode information carries the hierarchy.\n\nThis captures the current implementation, not a replacement identity. The descriptive direction was confirmed during documentation. Depth is recorded as observed, not imposed as a new doctrine. Sources are `gui/src/theme.ts`, `gui/src/style.css`, `gui/src/main.tsx` and the installed Mantine 9.8.2 defaults. Synthetic desktop, tablet, phone and reflow captures were regenerated with `python gui/e2e/smoke.py`; desktop, phone and episode captures were visually inspected. No UI code changed in this pass.",
    "keyCharacteristics": ["Compact controls and small corners.", "Plain text evidence, readable paths and restrained teal accents.", "A responsive lifecycle board with a separate inspection view."],
    "rules": [],
    "dos": ["Do retain the compact, utilitarian component character.", "Do use functional color names and distinguish authored tokens from Mantine defaults.", "Do preserve visible labels, native buttons and wrapping paths.", "Do keep stage, presence and verification meaning in text rather than color alone."],
